# CODEOWNERS — ownership-zone review routing (active under DL-051 zone structure)
# Listed owners are REQUIRED reviewers for changes under each path.
#
# ZONE SPLIT (velocity + control): engineering self-merges pure app code; the owner gates canon.
#  - `code/**` is INTENTIONALLY UNLISTED — it has no required code-owner, so a PR touching only
#    code/** merges on green CI alone (six-gate + visual-regression). This is "engineering authors
#    realization" (DL-051); the gates are the automated review.
#  - Everything canon/governance/design below requires the owner (@idris-manley). The 20_handoff
#    seam and CI/infra require both. A PR that touches ANY listed path needs that path's reviewer,
#    so cross-zone merges (e.g. the #113 integration, which conflicts against canon) stay owner-gated.
#
# RULESET REQUIREMENT for self-merge to work: `protect-main` must require "status checks to pass"
# + "review from Code Owners", with **required approvals = 0** (approvals are branch-wide and would
# otherwise re-gate code/**). Code-owner review still forces owner sign-off on the listed paths.
#
# Semantics (DL-051): 00_owner = owner-only; 10_product = product-authoritative; 20_handoff =
# CO-GOVERNED SEAM (both sides); 30_engineering = engineering-authoritative (owner still ratifies
# canon); 90_research = non-canonical. CODEOWNERS enforces REVIEW, not ratification — canonical
# changes route through Framework 001; only the owner ratifies/supersedes/adopts canon.

# --- 00_owner — owner only (doctrine, constitution, frameworks, decisions, glossary, TBD) ---
